title: Election of the Speaker of the House
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: speaker_election_needed = 1
priority: -1
on-arrival: {!
    Q.speaker_election_needed = 0;

    Q.previous_speaker = Q.speaker;
    Q.previous_speaker_party = Q.speaker_party;

    if (Q.house_majority >= 1) {
        Q.speaker_control = "rep";
    }
    else if (Q.rep_lib_working_majority == 1 && Q.liberal_split == 1) {
        Q.speaker_control = "coalition";
    }
    else if (Q.dem_r > Q.rep_r) {
        Q.speaker_control = "dem";
    }
    else {
        Q.speaker_control = "contested";
    }

    // In a contested House, the largest minor bloc decides who gets the gavel
    Q.speaker_kingmaker = "";
    if (Q.speaker_control === "contested") {
        if (Q.liberal_split == 1 && Q.lib_r > Q.rad_r && Q.lib_r >= Q.other_r) {
            Q.speaker_kingmaker = "liberal";
        }
        else if (Q.radical_split == 1 && Q.rad_r > Q.lib_r && Q.rad_r >= Q.other_r) {
            Q.speaker_kingmaker = "radical";
        }
        else {
            Q.speaker_kingmaker = "other";
        }
    }
!}

= Election of the Speaker

[? if previous_speaker != "" and speaker_control != "dem" : [+ previous_speaker +] has held the gavel until now, but a new Congress means a new vote. ?][? if previous_speaker != "" and speaker_control = "dem" : [+ previous_speaker +] has held the gavel until now, but the new Congress will not return it to him. ?]

[? if speaker_control = "rep" : With a Republican majority in the House, the choice of Speaker is ours to make. The Speaker sets the legislative agenda, assigns the committee chairmanships, and decides which bills ever reach the floor. This is not a ceremonial choice. ?]

[? if speaker_control = "coalition" : No party holds an outright majority in the House, but the <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republicans**</span> and <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> together command enough votes to organize the chamber. The gavel can be ours, but the Liberals will expect a say in who holds it, and they will not forget it if we ignore them. ?]

[? if speaker_control = "contested" : No party commands a majority, and the chamber cannot organize itself without help from the smaller blocs. The Speakership will go to whoever can assemble the votes, and every bloc knows its price. ?][? if speaker_kingmaker = "liberal" : The <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> hold the balance, and their votes will decide who can organize the House. ?][? if speaker_kingmaker = "radical" : The <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> hold the balance, and their votes will decide who can organize the House. ?][? if speaker_kingmaker = "other" : The minor parties and independents hold the balance, and each of them is bargaining for something. ?]

[? if speaker_control = "dem" : The new Congress convenes with the <span style="color: [+ dem_color+];">**[+ dem_name +]**</span> holding the largest bloc in the House, and the Speaker's chair belongs to them. We can nominate no candidate of our own. The Speaker will assign the chairmanships, control the calendar and decide which of our bills ever see a vote, and we will watch from the minority benches. ?]

- @Colfax
- @Stevens
- @Blaine
- @Dawes
- @Garfield
- @Washburne
- @keep_speaker: Keep the current Speaker.
- @dem_speaker_note

@Colfax
title: Schuyler Colfax (Indiana)
subtitle: [? if speaker = "Colfax" : Currently serving: retain him ?][? if speaker != "Colfax" : Moderate Republican. Affable, well-liked across factions. ?]
view-if: year <= 1869 and speaker_control != "dem"
on-arrival: {!
    let wasSpeaker = (Q.speaker === "Colfax");
    Q.speaker = "Colfax";
    Q.speaker_party = "Rep";

    if (!wasSpeaker) {
        Q.moderate_strength += 4;
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 3;
        if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
            Q.radical_relation -= 2;
        } else {
            Q.radical_dissent += 2;
        }
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 2;
        Q.liberal_dissent -= 2;
        Q.middle_class_rep += 2;
    } else {
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 2;
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 1;
    }

    Q.speaker_boosted_committee = "fiscal_policy";
    Q.speaker_boost_amount = 2;
!}
go-to: speaker_end

Schuyler Colfax, the "Smiler," is elected Speaker. His warmth and his talent for building consensus have made him popular across the party's <span style="color: #9D2933;">**moderate**</span> and <span style="color: #B5651D;">**conservative**</span> wings, and few members have a bad word to say about him.

[? if radical_split = 0 : The <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> tolerate him, if they do not love him. ?]

[? if radical_split = 1 : The breakaway <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republican Party**</span> has no particular love for him either, though he is no longer their problem to solve. ?]

[? if speaker = "Colfax" : Colfax continues his tenure, and the House settles back into its familiar rhythms under his steady hand. ?]

His allies on Ways and Means will smooth the path for tariff legislation.

@Stevens
title: Thaddeus Stevens (Pennsylvania)
subtitle: [? if speaker = "Stevens" : Currently serving ?][? if speaker != "Stevens" : Radical choice. Turns the speakership into a weapon for Reconstruction. ?]
view-if: year <= 1868 and stevens_advisor = 1 and stevens_dead != 1 and radical_split = 0 and speaker_control = "rep"
on-arrival: {!
    let wasSpeaker = (Q.speaker === "Stevens");
    Q.speaker = "Stevens";
    Q.speaker_party = "Rep";

    if (!wasSpeaker) {
        Q.moderate_dissent += 5;
        Q.conservative_dissent += 8;
        Q.radical_strength += 8;
        Q.radical_dissent -= 6;
        Q.liberal_dissent += 4;
        Q.freemen_rep += 4;
        Q.rural_dem -= 2;
    } else {
        Q.radical_strength += 2;
        Q.radical_dissent -= 2;
        Q.conservative_dissent += 2;
    }

    Q.speaker_boosted_committee = "civil_rights";
    Q.speaker_boost_amount = 3;
!}
go-to: speaker_end

Thaddeus Stevens takes the Speaker's chair like a force of nature. His iron grip on the floor and on committee assignments turns the chamber into an engine of Radical Reconstruction. The <span style="color: [+ dem_color+];">**[+ dem_name +]**</span> are apoplectic, the <span style="color: #B5651D;">**Conservative Republicans**</span> are alarmed, and the <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> are finally satisfied.

His allies on the Reconstruction Committee will move civil rights legislation at a speed no other Speaker could match.

@Blaine
title: James Blaine (Maine)
subtitle: [? if speaker = "Blaine" : Currently serving ?][? if speaker != "Blaine" : Ambitious moderate. Strong legislator, eye on the presidency. ?]
view-if: year >= 1868 and speaker_control != "dem"
on-arrival: {!
    let wasSpeaker = (Q.speaker === "Blaine");
    Q.speaker = "Blaine";
    Q.speaker_party = "Rep";

    if (!wasSpeaker) {
        Q.moderate_strength += 5;
        Q.conservative_strength += 3;
        if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
            Q.radical_relation -= 4;
        } else {
            Q.radical_dissent += 4;
        }
        Q.liberal_dissent -= 2;
        Q.middle_class_rep += 3;
    } else {
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 2;
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 1;
    }

    Q.speaker_boosted_committee = "fiscal_policy";
    Q.speaker_boost_amount = 2;
!}
go-to: speaker_end

James Blaine of Maine takes the gavel. Energetic, politically cunning and already building a national following, he is a gifted floor manager who consolidates the <span style="color: #9D2933;">**moderate**</span> and <span style="color: #B5651D;">**conservative**</span> wings behind him almost at once.

[? if speaker = "Blaine" : Blaine's grip on the chamber is firmer than ever. ?]

His ambitions, however, reach well beyond the Speakership, and it would be wise to keep an eye on him.

@Dawes
title: Henry Dawes (Massachusetts)
subtitle: [? if speaker = "Dawes" : Currently serving ?][? if speaker != "Dawes" : Fiscal conservative, known for probity and reform sympathies. ?]
view-if: year >= 1867 and speaker_control != "dem"
on-arrival: {!
    let wasSpeaker = (Q.speaker === "Dawes");
    Q.speaker = "Dawes";
    Q.speaker_party = "Rep";

    if (!wasSpeaker) {
        Q.conservative_strength += 5;
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 4;
        if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
            Q.radical_relation -= 5;
        } else {
            Q.radical_dissent += 5;
        }
        Q.liberal_dissent -= 3;
        Q.moderate_dissent += 2;

        Q.middle_class_rep += 4;
        Q.workers_rep -= 2;
    } else {
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 2;
        Q.liberal_dissent -= 1;
    }

    Q.speaker_boosted_committee = "monetary_policy";
    Q.speaker_boost_amount = 2;
!}
go-to: speaker_end

Henry Dawes brings a reputation for financial integrity and reform sympathies to the Speakership. His selection satisfies the <span style="color: #B5651D;">**conservative**</span> and <span style="color: #DAA520;">**liberal**</span> factions, who see in him a counterweight to Radical excess.

[? if radical_split = 0 : The <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radicals**</span> distrust him. ?]

[? if radical_split = 1 : The breakaway <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republican Party**</span> distrusts him, and is unsurprised that the regular organization would pick a counterweight to everything it stood for. ?]

Working men, sensing that he will not be their champion, drift slightly away from the party.

His Speakership strengthens fiscal oversight and speeds currency and banking legislation through committee.

@Garfield
title: James A. Garfield (Ohio)
subtitle: [? if speaker = "Garfield" : Currently serving ?][? if speaker != "Garfield" : Rising star. War hero, moderate Radical, skilled debater. ?]
view-if: year >= 1869 and speaker_control != "dem"
on-arrival: {!
    let wasSpeaker = (Q.speaker === "Garfield");
    Q.speaker = "Garfield";
    Q.speaker_party = "Rep";

    if (!wasSpeaker) {
        Q.moderate_strength += 4;
        if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
            Q.radical_relation += 2;
        } else {
            Q.radical_dissent -= 2;
        }
        Q.conservative_dissent += 1;
        Q.liberal_dissent -= 1;

        Q.workers_rep += 2;
        Q.rural_rep += 2;
        Q.freemen_rep += 2;
    } else {
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 2;
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 1;
    }

    Q.speaker_boosted_committee = "civil_rights";
    Q.speaker_boost_amount = 2;
!}
go-to: speaker_end

James Garfield, the self-made man from Ohio and celebrated Union general, carries credibility with both the <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical**</span> and <span style="color: #9D2933;">**moderate**</span> wings. A gifted orator, he commands the floor with natural authority.

[? if radical_split = 1 : Even the breakaway <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republican Party**</span> regards him as one of the few men left in the regular organization it can still work with. ?]

His broad appeal lowers factional friction and clears the way for Reconstruction-minded legislation.

@Washburne
title: Elihu Washburne (Illinois)
subtitle: [? if speaker = "Washburne" : Currently serving ?][? if speaker != "Washburne" : Reliably loyal, limited ambition, strong in foreign affairs. ?]
view-if: year >= 1866 and year <= 1872 and speaker_control != "dem"
on-arrival: {!
    let wasSpeaker = (Q.speaker === "Washburne");
    Q.speaker = "Washburne";
    Q.speaker_party = "Rep";

    if (!wasSpeaker) {
        Q.moderate_strength += 3;
        Q.conservative_strength += 2;
        if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
            Q.radical_relation -= 1;
        } else {
            Q.radical_dissent += 1;
        }
        Q.liberal_dissent += 2;

        Q.uk_relation += 2;
    } else {
        Q.moderate_dissent -= 1;
        Q.conservative_dissent -= 1;
    }

    Q.speaker_boosted_committee = "judiciary";
    Q.speaker_boost_amount = 2;
!}
go-to: speaker_end

Elihu Washburne, a close political ally of Grant from Illinois, takes the gavel. Reliable, unflashy, and content to serve the party rather than himself, he keeps the caucus orderly and the floor quiet.

His long interest in foreign affairs opens new diplomatic avenues, and his friendship with the General keeps the House and the Executive on good terms.

@keep_speaker
title: Retain [+ speaker +] as Speaker.
subtitle: Continuity has its value.
view-if: speaker != "" and speaker_party != "Dem" and speaker_party != "NCP" and speaker_control != "dem"
on-arrival: {!
    Q.moderate_dissent -= 1;
    Q.conservative_dissent -= 1;

    // The Speaker keeps the same committee priority as before
    if (Q.speaker_boosted_committee === undefined || Q.speaker_boosted_committee === "") {
        Q.speaker_boosted_committee = "fiscal_policy";
        Q.speaker_boost_amount = 2;
    }
!}
go-to: speaker_end

The House re-elects [+ speaker +] without controversy. The members know his habits, the committees know their chairmen, and no one sees a reason to disturb an arrangement that works.

@dem_speaker_note
title: Watch the House organize without us.
subtitle: The <span style="color: [+ dem_color+];">**[+ dem_name +]**</span> choose the Speaker.
view-if: speaker_control = "dem"
go-to: dem_speaker

@dem_speaker
on-arrival: {!
    let wasOpposition = (Q.speaker_party === "Dem" || Q.speaker_party === "NCP");

    // Michael Kerr (elected 1875, died in 1876) or Samuel Randall (elected late 1876)
    if (Q.year >= 1876) {
        Q.speaker = "Randall";
    } else {
        Q.speaker = "Kerr";
    }
    Q.speaker_party = (Q.ncp_founded == 1) ? "NCP" : "Dem";

    if (!wasOpposition) {
        // We have just lost the chamber
        if (Q.radical_split == 1) {
            Q.radical_relation -= 5;
        } else {
            Q.radical_dissent += 5;
        }
        Q.moderate_dissent += 3;
        Q.conservative_dissent += 2;

        // Reconstruction support is recalculated every month, so the cost is
        // applied to the persistent political cost penalty instead of the support itself
        Q.PoliticalCostPenalty = (Q.PoliticalCostPenalty || 0) + 10;
    } else {
        Q.moderate_dissent += 1;
    }

    Q.speaker_boosted_committee = "";
    Q.speaker_boost_amount = 0;
!}
go-to: speaker_end

The <span style="color: [+ dem_color+];">**[+ dem_name +]**</span> hold the House, and [+ speaker +] takes the gavel as Speaker.

[? if speaker = "Kerr" : Michael Kerr of Indiana is a lawyer of the old school, a defender of hard money and a steady opponent of Reconstruction measures. He does not need to be aggressive. He only needs to be in the chair. ?][? if speaker = "Randall" : Samuel Randall of Pennsylvania is a tough parliamentary tactician, a protectionist and a harsh critic of the administration. He knows the House rules better than anyone, and he knows exactly how to use them. ?]

Our legislative agenda is now effectively blocked. Bills that reach the floor will be shaped by <span style="color: [+ dem_color+];">**[+ dem_name +]**</span> priorities, not ours.

This is the price of losing the House. Reconstruction stalls, our chairmanships are stripped, and we can oppose but we cannot govern.

@speaker_end
title: Finish Voting
on-arrival: {!
    Q.speaker_election_needed = 0;

    // Republicans who organize a House without a majority of their own pay for it
    if (Q.speaker_control === "coalition") {
        Q.liberal_strength += 2;
        Q.liberal_dissent -= 3;
        Q.conservative_dissent += 1;
    }
    else if (Q.speaker_control === "contested") {
        if (Q.speaker_kingmaker === "liberal") {
            Q.liberal_strength += 3;
            Q.liberal_dissent -= 3;
            Q.conservative_dissent += 2;
        }
        else if (Q.speaker_kingmaker === "radical") {
            Q.radical_relation += 3;
            Q.conservative_dissent += 3;
            Q.moderate_dissent += 2;
        }
        else {
            Q.PoliticalCostPenalty = (Q.PoliticalCostPenalty || 0) + 2;
            Q.corruption += 1;
        }
    }
!}

The election of [+ speaker +] as Speaker is complete.

[? if speaker_control = "coalition" : The <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> have delivered the votes we needed, and they will expect their price to be paid in committee seats and influence. ?]

[? if speaker_control = "contested" and speaker_kingmaker = "liberal" : The <span style="color: #DAA520;">**Liberal Republicans**</span> have sold their votes dearly, and they leave with several chairmanships and a promise of influence. ?]

[? if speaker_control = "contested" and speaker_kingmaker = "radical" : The <span style="color: #7A1F5C;">**Radical Republicans**</span> have named their price, and the party's moderates are not happy about the bargain. ?]

[? if speaker_control = "contested" and speaker_kingmaker = "other" : The minor parties and independents have extracted patronage and committee seats in return for their votes, and the bargain was not a clean one. ?]

[? if speaker_boosted_committee = "fiscal_policy" : The new Speaker's allies on Ways and Means will smooth the path for fiscal and tariff legislation. ?]
[? if speaker_boosted_committee = "monetary_policy" : The new Speaker prioritizes currency and banking legislation, speeding it through committee. ?]
[? if speaker_boosted_committee = "civil_rights" : The new Speaker assigns a Reconstruction Committee favorable to our agenda, speeding civil rights legislation through the House. ?]
[? if speaker_boosted_committee = "judiciary" : The new Speaker keeps close watch on the courts and speeds judiciary reform through committee. ?]
[? if speaker_boosted_committee = "" : The committees now answer to the <span style="color: [+ dem_color+];">**[+ dem_name +]**</span>, and none of our legislation will be speeded through. ?]